# Local inventory

This private report is generated from local observations by `bash build_inventory.sh`.
An empty successful scan means no current members in its covered scope.
An incomplete scan keeps earlier observations stale and cannot authorize updates.

Existing reports and handwritten notes require an explicit migration preview:

```bash
bash build_inventory.sh --migration --preview
bash build_inventory.sh --migration --accept PROPOSAL_ID
```

The original bytes and their SHA-256 are backed up in private local state.
Legacy text is retained as orphan notes, separate from current installations.
Old tables, preferences and notes grant no update permission.

`bash build_inventory.sh --rebuild` collects again and preserves local notes and
identity-bound policy choices. A manual report edit blocks automatic replacement
until a new notes import preview is accepted.
